رَهَا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ وَلَوْ يَشَآءُ ٱللَّهُ لَٱنتَصَرَ مِنْهُمْ وَلَـٰكِن لِّيَبْلُوَا۟ بَعْضَكُم بِبَعْضٍ ۗ وَٱلَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا۟ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَلَن يُضِلَّ أَعْمَـٰلَهُمْ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"When you meet the disbelievers in battle, strike them in the neck, and once they are defeated, bind any captives firmly––later you can release them by grace or by ransom––until the toils of war have ended. That [is the way]. God could have defeated them Himself if He had willed, but His purpose is to test some of you by means of others. He will not let the deeds of those who are killed for His cause come to nothing;","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"فَإِذَا","en_gloss":"So when","transliteration":"fa-idhā","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":2,"ar":"لَقِيتُمُ","en_gloss":"you meet","transliteration":"laqītumu","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":4,"ar":"كَفَرُوا۟","en_gloss":"disbelieve","transliteration":"kafarū","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":5,"ar":"فَضَرْبَ","en_gloss":"then strike","transliteration":"faḍarba","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلرِّقَابِ","en_gloss":"the necks","transliteration":"l-riqābi","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":7,"ar":"حَتَّىٰٓ","en_gloss":"until","transliteration":"ḥattā","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":8,"ar":"إِذَآ","en_gloss":"when","transliteration":"idhā","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":9,"ar":"أَثْخَنتُمُوهُمْ","en_gloss":"you have subdued them","transliteration":"athkhantumūhum","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":10,"ar":"فَشُدُّوا۟","en_gloss":"then bind firmly","transliteration":"fashuddū","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱلْوَثَاقَ","en_gloss":"the bond","transliteration":"l-wathāqa","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":12,"ar":"فَإِمَّا","en_gloss":"then either","transliteration":"fa-immā","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":13,"ar":"مَنًّۢا","en_gloss":"a favor","transliteration":"mannan","verse_key":"47:4"},{"pos":14,"ar":"بَعْدُ","en_gloss":"afterwards","transliteration":"baʿdu","verse_ke